  Reading this table:
    median SNR  -- sd(real contrast) / sd(null contrast), median over
                   layer groups. 1.0 means the class is
                   indistinguishable from more retain data.
    above noise -- channels exceeding the null's 99th percentile,
                   pooled over groups. Pure noise gives about 1%.
    groups with < 32 channels are excluded from both.

====================================================================================================
RECOMMENDED FORGET CLASS
====================================================================================================
  ship (label 8)
    median SNR    16.090
    max SNR       47.540
    above noise   91.22%  (3970 of 4352 channels)
    strongest     fc (SNR 47.54, 98.8% above noise), layer4 (SNR 35.12, 95.3% above noise), layer1 (SNR 16.09, 45.3% above noise)

  For comparison, the instance-level forget set gave 0.55% above
  noise, against the 1.00% pure noise produces. Anything at or below
  1% here would mean class unlearning has no more structure to
  exploit than instance unlearning did, and the explanation on
  record is wrong.

